vendor/

# Generated/runtime
#
# Propel codegen output. Regenerate with `./propel <command>`; never commit.
# The exception is the model tree itself (src/Baja/Model), which propel.yaml.dist
# redirects into src/ and which IS committed — see docs/dev-workflow.md.
# generated-classes/ and generated-conf/ are Propel's defaults for that tree:
# they only appear if a propel command runs without picking up the config, and
# ignoring them stops a stray duplicate model tree being committed by accident.
# generated-migrations/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Unlike the rest of this
# list it is not regenerable output: `migration:diff` compares schema.xml
# against whatever database it is pointed at, so a migration deleted from the
# tree cannot be reproduced once the schema has moved on, and Propel tracks
# which migrations have been applied by their timestamps. It is a historical
# record, and reviewing it is already a step in the develop -> master checklist
# in docs/dev-workflow.md.
generated-sql/
generated-reversed-database/
generated-classes/
generated-conf/
*/cache/*
*/files/*
*.log

# Built by Baja\Api\GenerateDocs from the api/ tree; regenerate rather than
# commit, so it can never drift from the endpoints actually present.
baja-php/src/Baja/Api/ApiDocs.json

